  _signatureText: 'Every twelve seconds it fires spore pods at the fullest cluster of towers within its reach: three pads at most, and never more than about a quarter of your towers overgrown at once. An overgrown pad cannot be built on, and the tower on it fires at 70% while vines grow over it, until the growth is burned away. Rooted, it creeps along the road on growing roots; below half its health it tears itself out, walks faster and leaves rot behind it. It sinks into the bog and comes up at another bank.'
  _telegraphText: Roots spread at the bank of a bog over the three waves before it comes, and it grows out of that bog. Before a volley the flower opens its petals with a sweet rising sound, and the target pads glow green two seconds before the pods land.
  _counterText: 'Splash damage (cannon, mortar) that lands on a pad burns it clean, and the hero''s repair burns the vines off the tower it guards. The pods fly: air towers can shoot them down before they land. Do not stack all your towers in one cluster.'
